{"run_id": "planned-4192-s01-b81cb9", "t": 91.05, "tool": "pulls_open", "role": "open_pr", "args": {"issue": "issue-4192", "branch": "repomind/issue-4192", "title": "Re-enable the Export button after a failed export", "body": "File: src/components/ExportButton.tsx\n\nThe `handleClick` function in the `ExportButton` component sets `busy` to `true` at the start of the export process but only resets it to `false` in the `.then()` callback, which executes **only if the export succeeds**. If the export fails (e.g., due to a server error), the `busy` state remains `true`, disabling the button permanently. To fix this, the `exportReport` call should include a `.catch()` handler that also sets `busy` to `false`, ensuring the button is re-enabled after any export attempt, successful or not."}, "plan_step": 6, "key": "09fa9f718c2a67a48922fb85", "attempt": 1, "outcome": "ok", "is_error": false, "result": "{\"pull_request\": \"pr-19\", \"branch\": \"repomind/issue-4192\", \"state\": \"open\"}", "latency_s": 0.01, "cost_usd": 0.0}
